    <div class="prose">
      <p class="dropcap">I’m Fajar, a software engineer who likes understanding how things work beneath the surface.</p>
      <p>Lately, I’m making time to revisit the fundamentals: the concepts, patterns, and habits that make software reliable long after the excitement of a new tool wears off.</p>
      <p>AI is part of my toolkit, not a substitute for understanding. I use it to explore ideas, move faster, and challenge my assumptions — while keeping the foundations mine.</p>
      <p>This site is where I keep the useful parts of that process: notes that help me remember, projects that turn ideas into something real, and questions worth returning to. If a piece makes you pause and think, “that’s interesting,” then it’s doing its job.</p>
      <p>Start with the <a href="/blog/">writing archive</a> or see what I’m <a href="/projects/">building</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

